From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:59:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gud: bound TV mode reply length by the buffer size

With clang ThinLTO and -O3, linking gud.o fails:

  ld.lld: error: call to __read_overflow marked "dontcall-error":
  detected read beyond size of object (1st parameter)

gud_connector_add_tv_mode() kmallocs buf_len =
GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM * GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN bytes and
then walks ret / GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN names with a fortified
memchr(). usb_control_msg() never returns more than the requested
length, but that is not visible at this call site, so nothing bounds
num_modes by GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_MAX_NUM here. At -O3 the loop gets
unrolled and peeled, producing a memchr() at a constant offset past the
kmalloc() size, which FORTIFY_SOURCE turns into a hard link error.

Reject a reply longer than the buffer. This makes the bound explicit
(it also keeps modes[] from being indexed past MAX_NUM) and is a no-op
for any real device.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gud/gud_connector.c
@@ -390,7 +390,7 @@
 			  connector->index, buf, buf_len);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto free;
-	if (!ret || ret % GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN) {
+	if (!ret || ret > buf_len || ret % GUD_CONNECTOR_TV_MODE_NAME_LEN) {
 		ret = -EIO;
 		goto free;
 	}
